## November 12, 2026

### What I learned
Today, I explored Python strings, data types and basic operations.

Topics covered:
- `in` – checking whether an element or character exists in a sequence.
- `isinstance()` – checking whether a value belongs to a particular data type.
- `\n` – inserting a new line in a string.
- `len()` – getting the length of a string or collection.
- `index()` – finding the position of an element in a sequence.
- Negative indexing – accessing elements from the end of a sequence.
- Mutable vs. immutable values – understanding which data types can or cannot be modified after creation.
- String concatenation – combining strings using `+`.
- String interpolation – inserting variables or expressions into strings.

### What I practised
- Checking string membership.
- Working with string indexes.
- Exploring string manipulation.
- Combining strings and variables.

### Key takeaway
I learned how Python handles strings, how to access individual characters and how to work with different types of values.

